WEBVTT

cue0024648
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
of Rabbeinu Yonah. What is his name?

cue0024649
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
With Rabbe Udah, the son of the Rabbat.

cue0024650
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
I'm sorry, Rabbe Is'haq, the son of the Rabbat.

cue0024651
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
The son of the Rabbat, the arch-enemy of Al-Ambam,

cue0024652
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.000
is the teacher of...

cue0024653
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
What does it make it more Medusa?

cue0024654
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
The Gemariot are not as trustworthy as those of...

cue0024655
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Because it makes no sense.

cue0024656
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Wait!

cue0024657
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.000
I have patience.

cue0024658
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.000
What is the proof of Rabbeinu Yonah?

cue0024659
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.000
That the...

cue0024660
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.000
How do you know that this is...

cue0024661
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.000
How do you know that this is...

cue0024662
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Logic!

cue0024663
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.000
But how is it possible

cue0024664
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000
that Abba Yeh is going to be happy without a misbah?

cue0024665
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.000
How could he be happy outside the happiness of misbah?

cue0024666
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Bernie, you tell me what is he doing here?

cue0024667
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
I have to fill in.

cue0024668
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.000
All right, just a second. Go ahead.

cue0024669
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.000
What is he doing here?

cue0024670
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Very interesting. What is he doing here?

cue0024671
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.000
He is proving

cue0024672
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.000
that the Nusra of Sufah is better.

cue0024673
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.000
What is the basis?

cue0024674
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.000
An assumption.

cue0024675
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.000
What is the assumption?

cue0024676
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Point number three.

cue0024677
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.000
That you cannot be happy

cue0024678
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.000
outside the happiness of a misbah.

cue0024679
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.000
So you have two different points, which is interesting.

cue0024680
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.000
The first point, no?

cue0024681
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.000
You mentioned it first.

cue0024682
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.000
It says three.

cue0024683
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.000
The other is...

cue0024684
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Your point is the third.

cue0024685
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
But you said it first.

cue0024686
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Now, what is he saying?

cue0024687
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.000
We have two Nusraot.

cue0024688
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.000
The one from Sepharad, and the one from Sufah.

cue0024689
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.000
I'm going to prove

cue0024690
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.000
that one is better than the other.

cue0024691
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.000
And the basis of what?

cue0024692
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Of some sort of a logic that I am projecting.

cue0024693
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.000
The logic is

cue0024694
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.000
impossible to have happiness

cue0024695
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.000
outside the realm of the misbah.

cue0024696
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.000
You see?

cue0024697
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.000
So therefore, on the basis of this logic,

cue0024698
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.000
I am proving to you

cue0024699
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.000
that one Nusra

cue0024700
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.000
is superior to the other.

cue0024701
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.000
One minute.

cue0024702
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Let's analyze the methodology.

cue0024703
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.000
I'm going to prove

cue0024704
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.000
that one Nusra is better than the other.

cue0024705
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.000
Why?

cue0024706
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Because it is permitted to have happiness

cue0024707
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.000
outside the realm of misbah.

cue0024708
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.000
What would you say of this methodology?

cue0024709
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.000
In other words, part of being a Tamiha Khan is what?

cue0024710
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.000
What I call critical knowledge.

cue0024711
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.000
Among Sefaradim.

cue0024712
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.000
That's a very important thing.

cue0024713
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Here is the Nusra of the Gemaraʾ.

cue0024714
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.000
What is authoritative is the manuscript itself.

cue0024715
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.000
If this is an ancient manuscript,

cue0024716
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.000
whether you understand it or not,

cue0024717
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.000
that's irrelevant.

cue0024718
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.000
You deal with the data in front of you.

cue0024719
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.000
If we think to a logic.

cue0024720
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Here is the logic.

cue0024721
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Bring in a thousand logics.

cue0024722
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.000
This is the Gemaraʾ, Bino Hanan El.

cue0024723
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.000
Bino Hanan El receives from Rabia Gaon.

cue0024724
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.000
Rabia Gaon from Sharia Gaon.

cue0024725
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.000
Sharia Gaon from Rabia Bina Bina Bashir, eventually.

cue0024726
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.000
All the logic in the world.

cue0024727
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.000
Interesting.

cue0024728
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Suppose you have a Kusha.

cue0024729
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.000
That makes logic too.

cue0024730
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.000
I'm showing two methodologies.

cue0024731
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.000
In the case of Hakeem Es-Saffat,

cue0024732
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.000
always they changed the Gemaraʾ.

cue0024733
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Yes, it came from the logic.

cue0024734
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.000
It makes no sense.

cue0024735
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.000
From the Yeshiḇa of Rabia Bina Bina Bashir.

cue0024736
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.000
They had, they knew.

cue0024737
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.000
Not that he assumed that he had the correct one.

cue0024738
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.000
No.

cue0024739
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.000
It makes more sense.

cue0024740
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.000
It means.

cue0024741
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.000
The Nusra of Hakeem Es-Saffat.

cue0024742
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.000
It's more precise.

cue0024743
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.000
So absolutely he believed it was edited.

cue0024744
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.000
For a good reason.

cue0024745
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.000
It was edited for a good reason.

cue0024746
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.000
Why? Because it makes no sense.

cue0024747
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.000
So we said that Rabia Bina Bina Bashir is introducing three major rules here.

cue0024748
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.000
Number one.

cue0024749
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.000
The Nusra of Hakeem Es-Saffat is an authoritative point.

cue0024750
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.000
And therefore we know the reason for it is because it makes more sense.

cue0024751
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.000
Right.

cue0024752
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.000
So that's one point.

cue0024753
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.000
Point number two.

cue0024754
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.000
The presupposition.

cue0024755
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Why does it make no sense?

cue0024756
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.000
Because you cannot have happiness outside.

cue0024757
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Yes.

cue0024758
00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.000
So he's introducing a new idea.

cue0024759
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.000
Happiness is not permitted outside the realm of the Muslim.

cue0024760
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.000
And I said there is a third.

cue0024761
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:48.000
There is a third revolutionary idea that he's presenting.

cue0024762
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.000
What's the third point?

cue0024763
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.000
It's a revolutionary point that he's presenting.

cue0024764
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.000
You see.

cue0024765
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.000
Three revolutionary ideas presented by Rabbeinu Yonah.

cue0024766
00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.000
What's the third idea that he's presenting?

cue0024767
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.000
That you can't be happy outside of the Muslim.

cue0024768
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.000
No.

cue0024769
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.000
He said it.

cue0024770
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.000
That's one idea.

cue0024771
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.000
Point number two.

cue0024772
00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.000
All right.

cue0024773
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.000
What is the third revolutionary idea?

cue0024774
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.000
That he didn't put on tefillin.

cue0024775
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.000
Yeah. All right.

cue0024776
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.000
No, I'm saying.

cue0024777
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.000
The actual fact that because he didn't even put it on for a second even.

cue0024778
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.000
You know what I mean?

cue0024779
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.000
No.

cue0024780
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.000
No.

cue0024781
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.000
What he's saying is that a person who is sick may not put tefillin.

cue0024782
00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.000
A person who is clean cannot control his bowel movements.

cue0024783
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.000
That is written in the Gemaraʾ.

cue0024784
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.000
It's not in the Rabbeinu Yonah.

cue0024785
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.000
Again.

cue0024786
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.000
Yeah.

cue0024787
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.000
All right.

cue0024788
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.000
From the beginning?

cue0024789
00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.000
No, no, no.

cue0024790
00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.000
Continue.

cue0024791
00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.000
Yes.

cue0024792
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.000
It must be that also he said that I'm wearing tefillin.

cue0024793
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Okay.

cue0024794
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.000
Now he says why.

cue0024795
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.000
What does he know this for?

cue0024796
00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.000
One second.

cue0024797
00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.000
What does he know?

cue0024798
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:04.000
He is putting words in the mouth of our Yeh, which is not in the Gemaraʾ.

cue0024799
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:13.000
In other words, not only that Nosach is changed, but also you add to the words of the Gemaraʾ.

cue0024800
00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.000
This whole story.

cue0024801
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.000
This is a story that I was sick and I was sick.

cue0024802
00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.000
This whole story.

cue0024803
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:26.000
This is a story that I was sick and I had diarrhea and I was unable to wear tefillin.

cue0024804
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:31.000
Although the theory is correct, if a person has diarrhea, they cannot control his bowel movements,

cue0024805
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.000
he's not able to wear tefillin.

cue0024806
00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.000
There's no source.

cue0024807
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.000
It's an assumption.

cue0024808
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.000
That assumption is correct.

cue0024809
00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.000
There's no source.

cue0024810
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.000
There is source for this assumption.

cue0024811
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.000
There is?

cue0024812
00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.000
But not in the words of our Yeh.

cue0024813
00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:45.000
He's putting this, he's re-editing what the Gemaraʾ says.

cue0024814
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.000
The Gemaraʾ doesn't say one word about it.

cue0024815
00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:53.000
Our Yeh says only, the teacher doesn't, he doesn't say anything.

cue0024816
00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:56.000
Or if he says, even according to the Nosach of Sofat, he says,

cue0024817
00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.000
anate filim manahna.

cue0024818
00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:03.000
But doesn't say, anate filim manahna, because I was sick and so and so.

cue0024819
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.000
So one second.

cue0024820
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.000
One second, Jack.

cue0024821
00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.000
One second.

cue0024822
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:11.000
Here you have, here are your ideas.

cue0024823
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:18.000
Number one, the Nosach of Gemaraʾ that we receive from the Geonim could be, it stands for,

cue0024824
00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:24.000
the words within the Gemaraʾ are not the whole story.

cue0024825
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.000
You could add to it.

cue0024826
00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:32.000
And you could say, ah, why and what it means, because I had diarrhea.

cue0024827
00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:36.000
And number three is you cannot have a happiness outside the Yeh.

cue0024828
00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.000
This part about him having diarrhea.

cue0024829
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.000
Put it in here, or he just fabricated it.

cue0024830
00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.000
No.

cue0024831
00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.000
The Gemaraʾ says elsewhere.

cue0024832
00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.000
It says a person with diarrhea.

cue0024833
00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.000
But it doesn't mention about Yeh at all.

cue0024834
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.000
Okay, that's what I want to say.

cue0024835
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.000
It may not be fabricated.

cue0024836
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.000
No, he just said it.

cue0024837
00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.000
That's right, it's about the Gemaraʾ.

cue0024838
00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.000
All right?

cue0024839
00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.000
So therefore, this is the point.

cue0024840
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.000
Let's go back now into the Gemaraʾ itself.

cue0024841
00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.000
Who has my Gemaraʾ?

cue0024842
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.000
Now, we don't have to go back to Rabbani.

cue0024843
00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.000
Let's go back.

cue0024844
00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.000
How about, who was reading?

cue0024845
00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Can I ask a question then?

cue0024846
00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.000
Of course.

cue0024847
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.000
Because the Gemaraʾ that we have are Ashkenaziot.

cue0024848
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.000
All the Gemaraʾ that we have are Ashkenaziot.

cue0024849
00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.000
It was very difficult to find.

cue0024850
00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.000
Very, very difficult to find.

cue0024851
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.000
So what we're reading now...

cue0024852
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.000
Where does it say the part about Rabbeinu Yonah though?

cue0024853
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.000
It doesn't say it even.

cue0024854
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.000
They take it for granted.

cue0024855
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.000
Our Gemaraot are doctored.

cue0024856
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:46.000
Our Gemaraot are not the Gemaraot that Rambam read.

cue0024857
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.000
They're not.

cue0024858
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.000
But it doesn't say anything about Rabbeinu Yonah.

cue0024859
00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.000
It doesn't say anything about Rabbeinu having diarrhea.

cue0024860
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.000
No.

cue0024861
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.000
So that's a different version altogether.

cue0024862
00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.000
Yeah, well, no, no.

cue0024863
00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.000
No, Rabbeinu Yonah explains our Gemaraʾ.

cue0024864
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.000
He changes the Gissa of the Gemaraʾ.

cue0024865
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.000
Now this Gemaraot, the printer, forgets about the reef.

cue0024866
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.000
Brings already the Gissa of Rabbeinu Yonah.

cue0024867
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.000
One minute.

cue0024868
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.000
And the explanation...

cue0024869
00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.000
That's an explanation.

cue0024870
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.000
All right?

cue0024871
00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.000
Let's continue, because otherwise we're not going to have time.

cue0024872
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:21.000
But I'm saying, is there one other source or version?

cue0024873
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.000
Or there's many different versions?

cue0024874
00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.000
Jack, you have to let me lead the class.

cue0024875
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.000
All right, let's continue.

cue0024876
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.000
All right?

cue0024877
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.000
All of it is going to become clear by the Gemaraʾ itself.

cue0024878
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.000
I'm not going to say anything.

cue0024879
00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.000
Now, who wants to read?

cue0024880
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.000
Bernie, you read very little, no?

cue0024881
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.000
You read a little bit?

cue0024882
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.000
Go ahead, continue reading.

cue0024883
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.000
No, not mal.

cue0024884
00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.000
Mor.

cue0024885
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.000
Yes, always we say mor.

cue0024886
00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.000
Sefaradim say mor.

cue0024887
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.000
Mor vele deravina.

cue0024888
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.000
Sir.

cue0024889
00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.000
One second.

cue0024890
00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.000
Mor.

cue0024891
00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.000
The son of Rabbeinu Yonah.

cue0024892
00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.000
Rabbeinu Yonah was the...

cue0024893
